# Cargo build output. This covers lib/, app/, efi/ and any crate added later, together with
# everything written below it: the debug and release profiles, the headers cbindgen generates into
# lib/target/include, and the `cargo doc` output the documentation workflow copies out of
# lib/target/doc. The per-crate .gitignore files predate this one and are now redundant.
target/

# The lock files are deliberately *not* ignored. This repository ships binaries as well as a
# library, and the distribution packaging in debian/ and packaging/rpm/ resolves the dependencies
# with --locked against the vendored tree, so lib/Cargo.lock, app/Cargo.lock and efi/Cargo.lock are
# part of the source. See packaging/README.md.

# Backup files written by rustfmt.
*.rs.bk

# Debugging information produced by the MSVC builds of rustc.
*.pdb

# Coverage and profiling output. None of these tools is wired into the build, but they all write
# into the working tree when run by hand.
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
tarpaulin-report.html
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# Vendored Rust dependencies, created by packaging/vendor.sh. The tarballs that script produces are
# written to the parent directory and are therefore outside the repository.
/vendor/

# Local reproduction of the GitHub Pages job of .github/workflows/docs.yml.
/_site/

# Artefacts of a Debian package build in the working tree.
/debian/build/
/debian/cargo/
/debian/rustup/
/debian/tmp/
/debian/files
/debian/*.substvars
/debian/*.debhelper.log
/debian/.debhelper/
/debian/intel-crashlog/
/debian/intel-crashlog-efi/
/debian/libintel-crashlog1/
/debian/libintel-crashlog-dev/

# Crash Log records extracted from a live platform, which iclg names after the source device. They
# capture the state of the machine they were taken from, so they should not be committed by
# accident. The records under lib/tests/samples/ are synthetic fixtures and are named differently.
pmt:*.crashlog
*.crashlog.json

# Editor and operating system files. A personal global gitignore is the better place for these, but
# they turn up often enough in a shared checkout to be worth listing.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
/.idea/
/.vscode/
